+The paper table also reports route completion (all required goals reached), no-contact success (`success` and zero
+contacts of either kind), and median penalized time (the task timeout replaces unfinished trials). These are derived
+from existing trial rows; they do not change the frozen policies or simulator outcomes. The original completion-time
+column includes only route finishes, including those with contacts. With one scene, bootstrap intervals describe seed
+variation in that scene only. A zero-width interval after zero observed collisions is not evidence of zero population risk.
+
+## Running the selected scene set
+
+First run `e3_select_scenes.py` below and review its `selection.json`. Relative scene paths in that file are resolved
+against the project root. The selected prompt IDs and source scenes are fixed inputs to the suite, not replaced after
+observing simulation results. P18 was used for policy development; identify it as development data when reporting the
+remaining scenes as validation data. E3's worker/geometry tiers are separate from the source prompt's difficulty label.
+
+```
+uv run python scripts/e3_suite.py results/e3_scene_selection/selection.json --seeds 10 --out out/e3_suite_v1
+```
+
+Ten scenes x three tiers x ten paired seeds x three policies gives 900 planned trials. The runner reuses
+`e3_one_scene.py`, writes a log per scene, and verifies every expected (tier, seed, policy) row, worker count, variant,
+collision split, success definition, and frozen-policy provenance. Each scene must pass a replay rebuilt in a fresh
+world; `replay.json` records both trajectory/event digests. `suite.json` retains the selection, planned and verified trial
+counts, commands, and failed scenes. The runner continues to record scene failures, but runs `e3_analysis.py` only when
+the complete selection is verified and uses the same policy/code versions. Failed scenes are never silently omitted.
+
+Use a new, empty output directory for each run. Animations are omitted by default; add `--gif` for diagnostic GIFs.
+Missing or modified frozen policy provenance fails preflight before simulations. An invalid base variant stops that
+scene before hard variants are attempted; its static-check errors remain in the scene log and variant metadata.
+To pilot fewer scenes, create a separate reviewed selection with its own `n` and `chosen` list. The runner does not
+overwrite an earlier experiment or alter its selection. Existing E1 records and prototype results remain unchanged.
+
+Focused orchestration and reporting checks (no Isaac Sim needed):
+
+```
+uv run python tests/test_e3_suite.py
+uv run python tests/test_e3_reporting.py
+```
+
+The suite tests use controlled child-process results to check complete runs, missing/duplicate trials, replay failures,
+and failed-scene reporting. They do not substitute for an actual scene simulation or Isaac replay.
+
